			"notes": "# InvisTags 1.2.0\n\nThe first stable release of the two visibility toggles from the 1.1 beta. Both\nare **off by default** and can be changed at runtime from the config screen or\nwith `/invis`.\n\n## Gear reveal\n\nSome servers strip equipment packets so invisible players look completely\nempty. InvisTags remembers the gear your client actually saw and redraws it\nwhile the player is invisible — armour, main hand and off hand.\n\nToggle: **Reveal invisible players' armour and held items**, or `/invis gear true`.\n\n![GearBot wearing diamond gear](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MohenjoMC/Invistags/main/docs/screenshots/1.2.0/gear-visible.png)\n\n![Gear revealed while invisible](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MohenjoMC/Invistags/main/docs/screenshots/1.2.0/gear-reveal-on.png)\n\n![Same moment with gear reveal off](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MohenjoMC/Invistags/main/docs/screenshots/1.2.0/gear-reveal-off.png)\n\nThe last two screenshots are the same client and the same server tick, with the\nserver sending empty equipment in both. With the toggle off you see the bare\nskin — the armour in the middle image comes from the last-seen cache.\n\n## Vanished-player flag\n\nA player who is present in the world but missing from the tab list gets a red\n`[VANISHED]` suffix on their nametag and a one-time chat alert. Detection is\nskipped while the tab list is empty, so servers that hide the whole list do not\nproduce false positives.\n\nToggle: **Flag vanished players (no tab entry)**, or `/invis vanished true`.\n\n## Config and command\n\n![InvisTags config screen](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MohenjoMC/Invistags/main/docs/screenshots/1.2.0/config-screen.png)\n\n![In-game /invis status](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MohenjoMC/Invistags/main/docs/screenshots/1.2.0/status-command.png)\n\n`/invis` prints the current state; each option also takes `true`/`false`:\n\n```\n/invis skin|nametag|mobs|gear|vanished [true|false]\n/invis vanished list\n/invis remember [true|false]\n/invis config\n```\n\n## Compatibility\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Minecraft | 1.21.11, 26.1, 26.1.1, 26.1.2, 26.2, 26.3 |\n| Loader | Fabric Loader 0.19.3+ |\n| Required | Fabric API, Cloth Config |\n| Optional | Mod Menu |\n\nEach jar targets one game version — pick `1.21.11`, `26.1.2`, `26.2` or `26.3`\nfrom the files below.\n\n## Tested\n\n- 16 unit tests per version branch (config persistence, vanish-detection edge cases)\n- Client gametest on 1.21.11, 26.1.2, 26.2 and 26.3: real world, config screen, `/invis`\n- Two-player test: a modded client observes the Manchulla bot while the server\n  strips its gear and applies invisibility, with the toggle compared on and off\n\n## Notes and limits\n\n- Gear can only be restored once your client has seen it. Gear worn only while\n  invisible cannot be reconstructed.\n- Client-side only — no server plugin needed.\n- The vanished flag depends on the tab list; a server that hides it entirely\n  disables detection by design."
		},
